# CPU frequency governor selection.
#
# NOT STOCK — this whole file is ours. Nothing equivalent ships in revision 28.
#
# The kernel this device ships with (device/itel/S666LN-kernel) provides the
# `reflex` governor. Select it explicitly on both policies.
#
# THE TRIGGER MATTERS. Stock init.cgroup.rc — which this tree ships and stock's
# init.mt6789.rc imports — writes `sugov_ext` to these same two nodes in
# post-fs-data. Actions bound to one trigger run in the order init parsed them,
# which depends on import order, so competing writes in post-fs-data would be
# decided by something as fragile as a line's position in an import list.
# `on boot` fires strictly after `on post-fs-data`, so this write wins
# regardless.
#
# Measured on hardware, 2026-08-03:
#   scaling_available_governors (policy0 and policy6):
#     sugov_ext reflex conservative ondemand userspace powersave performance schedutil
# so sugov_ext is present on this kernel and init.cgroup.rc's write really does
# take effect — this is not a no-op being papered over. The previously shipped
# tree avoided the clash by dropping init.cgroup.rc entirely, losing its uclamp
# and boot-perf tuning with it.
#
# On a kernel without `reflex` the write below fails the way any bad
# scaling_governor write does — non-fatal, and the policy keeps whatever it had
# (sugov_ext from init.cgroup.rc, or the kernel default). That is deliberate:
# this file must not break a build that swaps the kernel out.
#
# policy0 = 6x Cortex-A55 (little), policy6 = 2x Cortex-A76 (big). Confirmed on
# hardware: policy0 related_cpus "0 1 2 3 4 5", policy6 "6 7", and those are the
# only two policies. Several stock rc files chown a policy4; they are generic
# MediaTek templates for a 4+4 SoC and the chown simply fails here.

on boot
    write /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_governor reflex
    write /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy6/scaling_governor reflex

    chown system system /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_governor
    chown system system /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy6/scaling_governor
    chmod 0660 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_governor
    chmod 0660 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy6/scaling_governor
